          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 2 — The Invisible Living World: Beyond Our Naked Eye"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.03,
            0.918,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "25"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.096,
            0.654,
            0.115
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Microorganisms can be beneficial or harmful to us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.116,
            0.822,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some microorganisms decompose the plant and animal waste into simple substances and clean up the environment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.153,
            0.823,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some microorganisms reside in the root nodules of legumes, such as peas, beans, and lentils. They trap nitrogen from the air and increase the soil fertility."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.203,
            0.821,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yeasts are fungi which are used in the process of making breads, cakes, pastries, idlis, dosas, and bhaturas."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.237,
            0.822,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Lactobacillus is used in the curd formation at home and fermentation process in food industry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.3,
            0.419,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep the curiosity alive"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.337,
            0.575,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Various parts of a cell are given below. Write them in the appropriate places in the following diagram. Nucleus Cytoplasm Chloroplast Cell wall Cell membrane Nucleoid"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.747,
            0.344,
            0.865,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Only in Animal Cell"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.588,
            0.338,
            0.941,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": [
            {
